{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte column definitions can contain strings or renderer functions that return primitive values, component configurations, or snippet configurations. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" component resolves those forms reactively with the correct cell or header context."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"flexrender-and-the-lower-level-form","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" and the Lower-Level Form"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte exports the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" component, not a separate lowercase "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" function. For normal table markup, import the component and pass exactly one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":" object:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { FlexRender } from '@tanstack/svelte-table'\n</script>\n\n{#each table.getHeaderGroups() as headerGroup (headerGroup.id)}\n  <tr>\n    {#each headerGroup.headers as header (header.id)}\n      <th>\n        {#if !header.isPlaceholder}\n          <FlexRender {header} />\n        {/if}\n      </th>\n    {/each}\n  </tr>\n{/each}\n\n{#each table.getRowModel().rows as row (row.id)}\n  <tr>\n    {#each row.getVisibleCells() as cell (cell.id)}\n      <td><FlexRender {cell} /></td>\n    {/each}\n  </tr>\n{/each}","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For cells, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" selects "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":" for aggregated rows, falls back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", and renders nothing for grouping placeholders. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<FlexRender footer={header} />"},{"type":"text","value":" for a footer-group header object."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"App tables created with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTableHook"},{"type":"text","value":" also expose "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" through the table and context-bound app components. The direct import shown above works for both ordinary and app tables."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The older lower-level component form accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":" explicitly:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<FlexRender content={cell.column.columnDef.cell} context={cell.getContext()} />","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefer the table-object shorthand because it makes the grouped-cell decisions for you."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"components-and-snippets-in-column-definitions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Components and Snippets in Column Definitions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wrap Svelte components with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderComponent()"},{"type":"text","value":" and snippets with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderSnippet()"},{"type":"text","value":" before returning them from a column renderer:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { renderComponent, renderSnippet } from '@tanstack/svelte-table'\n  import StatusCell from './StatusCell.svelte'\n  import { nameSnippet } from './snippets.svelte'\n\n  const columns = columnHelper.columns([\n    columnHelper.accessor('status', {\n      cell: ({ getValue }) =>\n        renderComponent(StatusCell, { status: getValue() }),\n    }),\n    columnHelper.accessor('name', {\n      cell: ({ getValue }) => renderSnippet(nameSnippet, getValue()),\n    }),\n  ])\n</script>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A snippet used with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderSnippet"},{"type":"text","value":" must accept one parameter. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" mounts the resulting component or invokes the snippet with the supplied props or parameter."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Placeholder headers remain the template's layout decision. Check "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header.isPlaceholder"},{"type":"text","value":" unless a spanning-header layout intentionally renders the placeholder."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"flexrender-and-the-lower-level-form","text":"FlexRender and the Lower-Level Form","level":2},{"id":"components-and-snippets-in-column-definitions","text":"Components and Snippets in Column Definitions","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nSvelte column definitions can contain strings or renderer functions that return primitive values, component configurations, or snippet configurations. The `FlexRender` component resolves those forms reactively with the correct cell or header context.\n\n## `FlexRender` and the Lower-Level Form\n\nSvelte exports the `FlexRender` component, not a separate lowercase `flexRender` function. For normal table markup, import the component and pass exactly one `cell`, `header`, or `footer` object:\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { FlexRender } from '@tanstack/svelte-table'\n</script>\n\n{#each table.getHeaderGroups() as headerGroup (headerGroup.id)}\n  <tr>\n    {#each headerGroup.headers as header (header.id)}\n      <th>\n        {#if !header.isPlaceholder}\n          <FlexRender {header} />\n        {/if}\n      </th>\n    {/each}\n  </tr>\n{/each}\n\n{#each table.getRowModel().rows as row (row.id)}\n  <tr>\n    {#each row.getVisibleCells() as cell (cell.id)}\n      <td><FlexRender {cell} /></td>\n    {/each}\n  </tr>\n{/each}\n```\n\nFor cells, `FlexRender` selects `aggregatedCell` for aggregated rows, falls back to `cell`, and renders nothing for grouping placeholders. Use `<FlexRender footer={header} />` for a footer-group header object.\n\nApp tables created with `createTableHook` also expose `FlexRender` through the table and context-bound app components. The direct import shown above works for both ordinary and app tables.\n\nThe older lower-level component form accepts `content` and `context` explicitly:\n\n```svelte\n<FlexRender content={cell.column.columnDef.cell} context={cell.getContext()} />\n```\n\nPrefer the table-object shorthand because it makes the grouped-cell decisions for you.\n\n## Components and Snippets in Column Definitions\n\nWrap Svelte components with `renderComponent()` and snippets with `renderSnippet()` before returning them from a column renderer:\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { renderComponent, renderSnippet } from '@tanstack/svelte-table'\n  import StatusCell from './StatusCell.svelte'\n  import { nameSnippet } from './snippets.svelte'\n\n  const columns = columnHelper.columns([\n    columnHelper.accessor('status', {\n      cell: ({ getValue }) =>\n        renderComponent(StatusCell, { status: getValue() }),\n    }),\n    columnHelper.accessor('name', {\n      cell: ({ getValue }) => renderSnippet(nameSnippet, getValue()),\n    }),\n  ])\n</script>\n```\n\nA snippet used with `renderSnippet` must accept one parameter. `FlexRender` mounts the resulting component or invokes the snippet with the supplied props or parameter.\n\nPlaceholder headers remain the template's layout decision. Check `header.isPlaceholder` unless a spanning-header layout intentionally renders the placeholder.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: FlexRender (Svelte) Guide\n---\n\nSvelte column definitions can contain strings or renderer functions that return primitive values, component configurations, or snippet configurations. The `FlexRender` component resolves those forms reactively with the correct cell or header context.\n\n## `FlexRender` and the Lower-Level Form\n\nSvelte exports the `FlexRender` component, not a separate lowercase `flexRender` function. For normal table markup, import the component and pass exactly one `cell`, `header`, or `footer` object:\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { FlexRender } from '@tanstack/svelte-table'\n</script>\n\n{#each table.getHeaderGroups() as headerGroup (headerGroup.id)}\n  <tr>\n    {#each headerGroup.headers as header (header.id)}\n      <th>\n        {#if !header.isPlaceholder}\n          <FlexRender {header} />\n        {/if}\n      </th>\n    {/each}\n  </tr>\n{/each}\n\n{#each table.getRowModel().rows as row (row.id)}\n  <tr>\n    {#each row.getVisibleCells() as cell (cell.id)}\n      <td><FlexRender {cell} /></td>\n    {/each}\n  </tr>\n{/each}\n```\n\nFor cells, `FlexRender` selects `aggregatedCell` for aggregated rows, falls back to `cell`, and renders nothing for grouping placeholders. Use `<FlexRender footer={header} />` for a footer-group header object.\n\nApp tables created with `createTableHook` also expose `FlexRender` through the table and context-bound app components. The direct import shown above works for both ordinary and app tables.\n\nThe older lower-level component form accepts `content` and `context` explicitly:\n\n```svelte\n<FlexRender content={cell.column.columnDef.cell} context={cell.getContext()} />\n```\n\nPrefer the table-object shorthand because it makes the grouped-cell decisions for you.\n\n## Components and Snippets in Column Definitions\n\nWrap Svelte components with `renderComponent()` and snippets with `renderSnippet()` before returning them from a column renderer:\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { renderComponent, renderSnippet } from '@tanstack/svelte-table'\n  import StatusCell from './StatusCell.svelte'\n  import { nameSnippet } from './snippets.svelte'\n\n  const columns = columnHelper.columns([\n    columnHelper.accessor('status', {\n      cell: ({ getValue }) =>\n        renderComponent(StatusCell, { status: getValue() }),\n    }),\n    columnHelper.accessor('name', {\n      cell: ({ getValue }) => renderSnippet(nameSnippet, getValue()),\n    }),\n  ])\n</script>\n```\n\nA snippet used with `renderSnippet` must accept one parameter. `FlexRender` mounts the resulting component or invokes the snippet with the supplied props or parameter.\n\nPlaceholder headers remain the template's layout decision. Check `header.isPlaceholder` unless a spanning-header layout intentionally renders the placeholder.\n"}
